  "riskWarningsAndDisadvantages": {
    "generalRiskWarnings": [
      {
        "text": "Unit prices and the value of your pension fund can fall as well as rise and there is no guarantee you will receive a return of your original capital, especially in the early years or if you choose to take an income from it.",
        "topic": "CapitalLoss",
        "isClientSpecific": false,
        "provenance": {
          "assertionStatus": "Stated",
          "pageNumbers": [
            12
          ],
          "sectionHeading": "Fund recommendation"
        }
      },
      {
        "text": "You are aware that investment values can rise as well as fall, and although your experience is limited to your workplace pension arrangements, you understand that returns are not guaranteed.",
        "topic": "InvestmentVolatility",
        "isClientSpecific": true,
        "provenance": {
          "assertionStatus": "Stated",
          "pageNumbers": [
            4
          ],
          "sectionHeading": "Capacity for loss"
        }
      },
      {
        "text": "You are aware that your funds may go up as well as down, and the higher risk you take with your funds, potential there is for larger drops in value.",
        "topic": "RiskDrops",
        "isClientSpecific": true,
        "provenance": {
          "assertionStatus": "Stated",
          "pageNumbers": [
            4
          ],
          "sectionHeading": "Attitude to Risk \u0026 Capacity for loss"
        }
      }
    ],
    "productSpecificRisks": [
      {
        "text": "Should you require access to these funds in the future it will usually take 10-15 working days for administration, disinvestment and banking processes to complete.",
        "topic": "AccessDelay",
        "isClientSpecific": false,
        "provenance": {
          "assertionStatus": "Stated",
          "pageNumbers": [
            8
          ],
          "sectionHeading": "Other Considerations of Switching"
        }
      },
      {
        "text": "Whilst the transactions are pending, there could be movements within the stock-market; that is to say that the stock-market could rise or fall in value. If the market rises in value between the date of realising your existing funds and the purchase of your new (funds), you could be financially disadvantaged insofar as the cost of buying your new fund could be greater. Conversely, if there is a fall in the market between the date of realising your existing funds and the purchase of your new funds, you could be financially advantaged insofar as the cost of buying your new funds could be lower.",
        "topic": "MarketTimingRisk",
        "isClientSpecific": false,
        "provenance": {
          "assertionStatus": "Stated",
          "pageNumbers": [
            8
          ],
          "sectionHeading": "Other Considerations of Switching"
        }
      }
    ],
    "investmentRisks": [
      {
        "text": "Your recommended Aviva advised funds have demonstrated stronger performance compared to your existing Aviva holdings. However, they have not outperformed your current Zurich funds. It\u0027s important to note that your Zurich investments are allocated to higher-risk funds, which are more susceptible to market volatility, resulting in greater fluctuations in value.",
        "topic": "PerformanceVariability",
        "isClientSpecific": true,
        "provenance": {
          "assertionStatus": "Stated",
          "pageNumbers": [
            13
          ],
          "sectionHeading": "Performance Assessment"
        }
      },
      {
        "text": "A switch between pension providers does not guarantee a greater pension fund at retirement and there is no guarantee that the new provider\u0027s funds will outperform those of your existing provider.",
        "topic": "NoPerformanceGuarantee",
        "isClientSpecific": false,
        "provenance": {
          "assertionStatus": "Stated",
          "pageNumbers": [
            12
          ],
          "sectionHeading": "Fund recommendation"
        }
      },
      {
        "text": "There is no guarantee the return on the new investment will be greater than that of your existing arrangement for these funds.",
        "topic": "NoOutperformanceGuarantee",
        "isClientSpecific": false,
        "provenance": {
          "assertionStatus": "Stated",
          "pageNumbers": [
            8
          ],
          "sectionHeading": "Other Considerations of Switching"
        }
      }
    ],
    "materialDisadvantages": [
      {
        "text": "Based on a mid-growth rate of 2.94%, including our advice fees, the recommended plan would need to grow by 4.8% per year up to age 75 in order to meet the same value as your current plan.",
        "topic": "CriticalYieldRequirement",
        "isClientSpecific": true,
        "linkedObjectiveIds": [
          "OBJ2"
        ],
        "provenance": {
          "assertionStatus": "Stated",
          "pageNumbers": [
            11
          ],
          "sectionHeading": "Pension Switch Charges Only Assessment",
          "quote": "the recommended plan would need to grow by 4.8% per year up to age 75 in order to meet the same value as your current plan"
        }
      },
      {
        "text": "As we have agreed to be remunerated via the policy (initial and ongoing), our calculations showed that the Aviva plan is 4.24% more expensive than your current plans. This means that your proposed plan will need to outperform your current plan by \u00A34,672 in the first year (in monetary terms).",
        "topic": "AdviserChargeImpact",
        "isClientSpecific": true,
        "provenance": {
          "assertionStatus": "Stated",
          "pageNumbers": [
            11
          ],
          "sectionHeading": "Pension Switch Charges Only Assessment",
          "quote": "the Aviva plan is 4.24% more expensive than your current plans"
        }
      },
      {
        "text": "Your funds are currently invested in lifestyling funds, which automatically reduce investment risk as you approach retirement. As a result, your portfolio will eventually move outside of your agreed risk range.",
        "topic": "LifestylingDrift",
        "isClientSpecific": true,
        "provenance": {
          "assertionStatus": "Stated",
          "pageNumbers": [
            7
          ],
          "sectionHeading": "My Recommendation",
          "quote": "Your funds are currently invested in lifestyling funds, which automatically reduce investment risk as you approach retirement. As a result, your portfolio will eventually move outside of your agreed risk range."
        }
      }
    ],
    "limitations": [
      {
        "text": "If you were to transfer all your pensions into this plan, it would limit how you can withdraw funds. In the future, this would be important to you, as you would be unable to access this pension flexibly.",
        "topic": "WithdrawalRestrictions",
        "isClientSpecific": true,
        "provenance": {
          "assertionStatus": "Stated",
          "pageNumbers": [
            6
          ],
          "sectionHeading": "My Recommendation"
        }
      },
      {
        "text": "Currently, Scottish Widows does not offer a single multi-asset fund that aligns with your risk rating of 5. To achieve this level of risk, we would need to combine two funds. One of which is entirely invested in money market (cash) holdings. This would effectively leave around 20-30% of your portfolio out of the market.",
        "topic": "FundRangeConstraint",
        "isClientSpecific": true,
        "provenance": {
          "assertionStatus": "Stated",
          "pageNumbers": [
            6
          ],
          "sectionHeading": "My Recommendation"
        }
      },
      {
        "text": "All other risks associated with this investment are detailed in the product literature provided to you. You should read this document carefully.",
        "topic": "RisksInProductLiterature",
        "isClientSpecific": false,
        "provenance": {
          "assertionStatus": "Stated",
          "pageNumbers": [
            8
          ],
          "sectionHeading": "Other Considerations of Switching"
        }
      }
    ],
